// IRIW (Independent Reads of Independent Writes), all-relaxed.
//
// rmm-zoo property: mca (Atomicity / Multicopy atomic).
// Source: Sarkar et al., "Understanding POWER Multiprocessors" (PLDI 2011);
//         Alglave, Maranget & Tautschnig, "Herding Cats" (TOPLAS 2014), Fig. 8;
//         Su & Colvin, "Weak Memory Model Formalisms" (CCPE 38(2), 2026), section 2.4.
//
// The two readers observe the two independent writes in OPPOSITE orders. No
// single global order of writes explains that, so this is the baseline
// non-multicopy-atomic shape. With no ordering at all between each reader's
// loads it is also witnessed by plain load-load reordering, which is why the
// dependency- and fence-carrying variants in this directory, not this one, are
// what actually isolate multicopy atomicity.
//
// Reference verdicts: SC forbids. x86-TSO / TSO / ARMv8 / RVWMO (MCA) forbid.
//                     POWER / ARMv7 / C11 / RC11 (non-MCA) allow.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x := 1
} ||| {
  y := 1
} ||| {
  r1 := x;
  r2 := y
} ||| {
  r3 := y;
  r4 := x
}
%%
allow (r1 = 1 && r2 = 0 && r3 = 1 && r4 = 0) [Power]
